{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact head d9a426d24500aa5ff2e3d74fc97db0632fcfe0f7. This verdict reviews the exploration instructions, not a positioning design or the future assets. The separate first-round answers are still owed and are being prepared.\n\nP2 — Make the naming constraint consistent with the actual note and the authorized constraint. notes/2026-10-02-positioning-exploration.md@d9a426d24500aa5ff2e3d74fc97db0632fcfe0f7 sections 2/H7 and 4/Q9 name the infrastructure provider, while sections 3 and 6 and artifact #9293 say there are no other named products, tools or companies. H5/H6 and the bases also name internal research projects and a separate protocol. Parent request #9291 allows ubiquitous names; this review invitation instead says GitHub only. These are different rules, and the note fails its own absolute rule. Repair the public wording to satisfy the tighter invitation, using “the hosting platform” where the provider name is unnecessary, and state explicitly whether exact source titles and repository paths in research evidence are exempt. If the intended constraint is broader than GitHub only, obtain and record that change rather than assert compliance with the narrower one. Validation: read every heading, hypothesis, question and output constraint together; the artifact report must describe the rule the resulting note actually meets.\n\nP2 — Ask for a falsifiable guarantee and implementation-boundary check, not only rewordings. Sections 2/H3/H6, 4/Q3/Q6/Q12 and 5 currently ask for wording alternatives, lifecycle mapping and evidence for H5, but never require the round to decide which of the platform claims are implemented, measured, proposed or unsupported, or under what conditions they hold. That omission can change the one claim and the platform-first choice. At this exact head, docs/protocol.md R-REV-1 to R-REV-3 let earlier evidence stop counting and obligations reopen; R-PUB-2/R-PUB-5 retain an unresolved external publication; R-ADM-1 excludes early failures from the permanent record. “What is decided stays decided” cannot silently mean evidence never changes, external effects always finish, or every submitted attempt is recorded. The present application also has fixed software-specific kinds, repository state and platform invariants: replacing a policy file alone has not been shown to produce an arbitrary game or business application. Add a required exploration question and return item that test H3/H6/H7 against those cases, identify the trusted components and the same-record/same-rules conditions for consistent state, and separate an immutable historical decision from current evidence, current state and confirmed external outcome. Require source locations and readiness labels for every proposed worked room, with one counterexample that would falsify the claim. This is a request to test the hypotheses, not to adopt different wording or reduce product scope.\n\nP2 — Keep the middle-room choice open through the specified output. Section 4/Q9 asks the round to choose among rollout, production access and case management, and Q10 asks for the chosen room’s rules. Section 7 nevertheless mandates a rollout rulebook appendix regardless of the choice. That precommits the next design and can bias a nominally breadth-first round. Change section 7 to require the chosen middle room’s rulebook, with rollout only if it wins, and allow rejection or deferral with reasons. Validation: a complete round selecting a different middle room must satisfy sections 5 and 7 without silently changing the instructions.\n\nArchitecture: documentation only; no runtime layer or architecture contract is changed. The instructions appropriately label all eight positions as hypotheses and postpone asset work. The missing boundary/readiness question above is material to the architecture claim, particularly the distinction between the implemented software application and a proposed general application platform.\nSecurity: no new executable trust boundary, credential or authority-bearing operation is introduced. Visibility is correctly excluded from the guarantee. The exploration must still examine the trust assumptions and compromised-evidence/publication cases before its guarantee is adopted.\nSimplification: the Q1–Q15 grouping and required alternatives give a useful, bounded breadth test. Keep that structure; reconcile the naming rules and the precommitted appendix, and add the missing truth/boundary test rather than expanding into a delivery plan.\n\nValidation: full positioning note and its sole changed-path diff read in a separate clean checkout /tmp/artroom-checker-position-v1 at d9a426d24500aa5ff2e3d74fc97db0632fcfe0f7; git diff --check against base 5822204f passed. Read the relevant plan workflow, API, onboarding and scope sections, and protocol terms, authority, landing, publication, revocation, policy and log sections at the same revision. No runtime code or guard changes; no runtime tests or mutation tests were run or claimed. Main moved to 77d2e6c5d17b954a442f0b09b1e951fc4e451c3d while reviewing; this is an exact-head verdict, not approval of that merge.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a10ed3a6ffe03b3624807b7d9dac1e7bf7c6ebd","binding":"assigned","head":"d9a426d24500aa5ff2e3d74fc97db0632fcfe0f7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:77e45a1653911ef9d90178acc336ccab6b6c25a0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0655d5dafb44587d1bcca17d0a96c15d295a2c36\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4a4d549bb3bb4f3481a22cf80c034eb274997a3a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}